  "timeframe": "Current state as of 2026-11-14T04:39:11Z",
  "criteria": "Check at least: notebook direct internet access enabled; root access enabled; notebook/endpoint/training volume and output KMS encryption (CMK vs none); inter-container traffic encryption; network isolation off for training/processing/models; jobs/models/endpoints not in a VPC; Studio domain AppNetworkAccessType (PublicInternetOnly) and EFS KMS encryption; overly permissive execution roles (AdministratorAccess, *:* policies, s3:*, iam:PassRole *); security groups with 0.0.0.0/0 ingress attached to SageMaker resources; endpoint data capture destination encryption; IMDSv2 enforcement on notebook instances (MinimumInstanceMetadataServiceVersion); lifecycle config risks; unencrypted or public S3 buckets used as SageMaker outputs if discoverable; absence of tagging if relevant; deprecated platform identifiers. Handle pagination fully. For each finding output a JSON object with fields: id, title, severity (CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/INFO), category, resource_type, resource_arn, region, account_id, description, evidence (the actual API field/value observed), recommendation, references (optional). Return: (1) summary counts by severity, (2) a concise human-readable table of findings, (3) a single JSON array containing EVERY finding object (do not omit or truncate any), (4) list of resource types checked with counts of resources, and any checks that could not be performed (e.g., AccessDenied) and why. If there are no SageMaker resources, say so explicitly and list the calls made."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Run read-only SageMaker security assessment in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

